  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="41.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 41.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ gyf he ladian wylle, ladige mid þryfealdan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41.1" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ gif he ladian wylle, hine ladige mid þryfealdan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="41.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et si se purgare uelit, tripliciter hoc faciat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="41.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ gyf he ladian wylle, ladie hine mid ðryfealdan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gyf he ladian wylle, ladige mid þryfealdan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And if he seeks to clear himself, he shall do so by the triple mode of proof.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And if he desires to exonerate himself, he must do so by the threefold oath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And if he wishes to clear himself, he is to clear himself with three-fold process of exculpation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn er sich jedoch rein schwören will, reinige er sich mit dreifachem [Beweise].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if he wishes to clear himself, let him clear himself with the threefold [proof].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="341"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_27-1">VIII Atr 27.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 27, 1</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_27-1">VIII Atr 27.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 41:1: VIII Atr 27:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><label>parallel</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_27-1">VIII Atr 27.1</ref> <quote>VIII Atr 27:1/II Cn 41:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="468"><label>from</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_27-1">VIII Atr 27.1</ref> <quote>VIII Ethelred, 27.1 (27 is not used by Cnut’s law).</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VIII Atr 27.1.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">VIII Ethelred, 27.1 (27 is not used by Cnut’s law). But Ethelred allowed either simple or triple oath according to the crime involved.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ladige mid: ladie hine mid B</note>
      </div>
